 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No motif on Musa, the prophets (20:13) or the Prophet ﷺ; no crown for «ملوكا» (they were not literal kings: «تملكون أمركم»). Footsteps for «ادخلوا». No fighting drawn. Their refusal (22) is glossed only as As-Sa'di's verdict on it. STAGING v4: 19 stays ambient: the Messenger coming to the People of the Book after a gap in the messengers (his coming and conduct cannot be staged without implying him), and Allah's power. 20-22: Musa is a blue drop with his name in the desert near the land (As-Sa'di: they had set out for it and come close); his people are a small group (3, no woman, as they refuse). Musa speaks on 20:2 and 21:1 and points ahead toward the land on 21:2 (footsteps plate for entering). A breaking-chain plate on 20:15 for being free after slavery to Pharaoh (both tafsirs), no crown. No motif or camera move on Musa or on the prophets (20:13); wide shots instead of pans for the label. The people answer on 22:1 and shake their heads on 22:8. The mighty people in the land are never drawn, no soldiers, no weapon and no fighting."
 },
